      en: 'Changes in the cartilage and joint of the hip causing groin or thigh pain, stiffness in the morning or after sitting, and difficulty with socks, shoes and stairs. Osteoarthritis does not mean the joint "wears away" with every movement — exercise is one of the most effective treatments.\n\nRehab relies on education, strengthening and control exercise, regular aerobic activity, and weight management where needed. Mild pain during exercise (up to 3–4/10) is acceptable if it settles within 24 hours.\n\nRefer to a doctor for sudden severe pain or inability to weight-bear, severe persistent night pain, fever, rapid functional decline, or no improvement after 3 months of consistent exercise with pain severely affecting daily life — for orthopaedic assessment.'
